content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Freelancer",
      "description": "Independent worker offering services"
    },
    {
      "name": "Profile",
      "description": "Freelancer Profile showing skills and experience",
      "attributes": [
        "Skill",
        "Experience"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Skill",
      "description": "Freelancer capability or expertise"
    },
    {
      "name": "Experience",
      "description": "Freelancer past work background"
    },
    {
      "name": "Project Proposal",
      "description": "Freelancer submission for a project",
      "attributes": [
        "Deadline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Deadline",
      "description": "Time by which work must be completed"
    },
    {
      "name": "Client",
      "description": "Person posting projects and hiring freelancers"
    },
    {
      "name": "Project Description",
      "description": "Client description of required work"
    },
    {
      "name": "Completed Work",
      "description": "Finished work delivered for a project"
    },
    {
      "name": "Contact",
      "description": "Communication exchange between Client and Freelancer"
    },
    {
      "name": "Feedback",
      "description": "Client evaluation of Completed Work",
      "attributes": [
        "Completed Work"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Payment",
      "description": "Money paid for Completed Work",
      "attributes": [
        "Completed Work"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Platform Manager",
      "description": "Administrator overseeing platform activity"
    },
    {
      "name": "Platform Guidelines",
      "description": "Rules for acceptable platform use"
    },
    {
      "name": "Verification",
      "description": "Platform Manager review of submissions"
    },
    {
      "name": "Dispute Report",
      "description": "Complaint raised about a conflict"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Freelancer Workspace": {
      "objects": [
        "Freelancer",
        "Profile",
        "Experience",
        "Skill",
        "Project Proposal",
        "Deadline"
      ]
    },
    "Client Commission": {
      "objects": [
        "Client",
        "Project Description"
      ]
    },
    "Project Execution": {
      "objects": [
        "Contact",
        "Completed Work",
        "Feedback",
        "Payment"
      ]
    },
    "Administration": {
      "objects": [
        "Platform Manager",
        "Verification",
        "Platform Guidelines",
        "Dispute Report"
      ]
    },
    "subdomain connections": [
      "Freelancer Workspace--Project Execution",
      "Client Commission--Project Execution",
      "Administration--Project Execution",
      "Administration--Freelancer Workspace",
      "Administration--Client Commission"
    ]
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
